# Part B — Gestalt grouping {#sec-part-b}

Perception does not stop at measuring single marks; it groups them. Marks that connect read as one structure, marks that flow read as a path, marks that sit close or look alike read as a cluster, and a boundary read as enclosure turns empty space into an encoding — these Gestalt principles are the load-bearing walls of the network, the Sankey, the heatmap and the map.

