A food web draws species as nodes and feeding as directed edges, so the trophic structure of a community becomes a graph read at a glance. Elton fixed the ecological concepts of the food chain and the niche [@elton1927animal], though the Bear Island survey of Summerhayes and Elton [@summerhayes1923contribution] had printed the connected web four years earlier.

